    "photon_energy": {
      "question": "Find the energy of a photon of wavelength 500 nm.",
      "answer": "3.97 × 10⁻¹⁹ J (2.48 eV)",
      "reply": "**Given**\n\n$\\lambda = 500\\,\\mathrm{nm}$  \n$\\lambda = 5 \\times 10^{-7}\\,\\mathrm{m}$\n\n**Find**\n\n$E$\n\n**Formula**\n\nPhoton-energy relation:\n\n$E = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda}$\n\n**Substitution**\n\n$E = \\frac{6.6261 \\times 10^{-34} \\cdot 299792458}{5 \\times 10^{-7}}$\n\n**Answer**\n\n```answer\n3.97 \\times 10^{-19}\\,\\mathrm{J}\\ (2.48\\,\\mathrm{eV})\n```\n"
    },
    "launch_angles": {
      "question": "At what angle must a projectile be launched at 20 m/s to land 30 m away?",
      "answer": "23.7° or 66.3°",
      "reply": "**Given**\n\n$v_0 = 20\\,\\mathrm{m/s}$\n\n$d = 30\\,\\mathrm{m}$\n\n$g = 9.81\\,\\mathrm{m/s²}$\n\n**Find**\n\n$\\theta$\n\n**Formula**\n\nProjectile-motion equation:\n\n$\\theta = \\tfrac{1}{2} \\arcsin\\!\\left(\\frac{Rg}{v_0^2}\\right)$\n\n$\\theta' = 90^\\circ - \\theta$\n\n**Substitution**\n\n$\\theta = \\tfrac{1}{2} \\arcsin\\!\\left(\\frac{30 \\cdot 9.81}{20^{2}}\\right)$\n\n**Answer**\n\n```answer\n23.7^\\circ\\ \\text{or}\\ 66.3^\\circ\n```\n"
    },
    "parallel_resistance": {
      "question": "Find the total resistance of 4 ohm, 6 ohm and 12 ohm resistors in parallel.",
      "answer": "2 Ω",
      "reply": "**Given**\n\n$R_1 = 4\\,\\Omega$\n\n$R_2 = 6\\,\\Omega$\n\n$R_3 = 12\\,\\Omega$\n\n**Find**\n\n$R_p$\n\n**Formula**\n\nParallel-resistance law:\n\n$\\frac{1}{R_p} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\frac{1}{R_3}$\n\n**Substitution**\n\n$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{12}$\n\n**Answer**\n\n```answer\n2\\,\\Omega\n```\n"
    },
    "rebound_impulse": {
      "question": "A 0.2 kg ball hits a wall at 10 m/s and rebounds at 8 m/s. Find the impulse.",
      "answer": "3.6 N·s (opposite to the initial motion)",
      "reply": "**Given**\n\n$m = 0.2\\,\\mathrm{kg}$\n\n$v_1 = 10\\,\\mathrm{m/s}$\n\n$v_2 = -8\\,\\mathrm{m/s}$\n\n**Find**\n\n$J$\n\n**Formula**\n\nImpulse-momentum theorem:\n\n$J = m(v_2 - v_1)$\n\n**Substitution**\n\n$J = 0.2 \\cdot ((-8) - 10)$\n\n**Answer**\n\n```answer\n3.6\\,\\mathrm{N·s}\\ (\\text{opposite to the initial motion})\n```\n"
    },
    "heater_energy": {
      "question": "A 2 kW heater runs for 3 hours. How much energy does it use in kWh?",
      "answer": "6 kWh",
      "reply": "**Given**\n\n$P = 2\\,\\mathrm{kW}$  \n$P = 2000\\,\\mathrm{W}$\n\n$t = 3\\,\\mathrm{h}$  \n$t = 10800\\,\\mathrm{s}$\n\n**Find**\n\n$E$\n\n**Formula**\n\nElectrical-energy formula:\n\n$E = P t$\n\n**Substitution**\n\n$E = 2000 \\cdot 10800$\n\n$ = 2.16 \\times 10^{7}\\,\\mathrm{J} = 6\\,\\mathrm{kWh}$\n\n**Answer**\n\n```answer\n6\\,\\mathrm{kWh}\n```\n"
    },
